            {"question":"Which blood pressure change is mentioned as an age-related cardiovascular change?","options":["Blood pressure decreases","Blood pressure remains unchanged","Blood pressure increases","Blood pressure disappears"],"answer":"Blood pressure increases"},
            {"question":"A nurse is caring for an elderly patient with cardiovascular changes. Which activity recommendation is MOST appropriate?","options":["Encourage excessive exercise","Avoid all exercise","Encourage moderate exercise according to individual tolerance","Encourage exercise without rest periods"],"answer":"Encourage moderate exercise according to individual tolerance"},
            {"question":"For an older adult with high blood pressure, the lecture recommends:","options":["A high-salt diet","Decreased fat intake and a low-salt diet","Avoiding all physical activity","Increasing fat intake"],"answer":"Decreased fat intake and a low-salt diet"},
            {"question":"Which respiratory change is expected with aging?","options":["Respiratory muscles become stronger","Respiratory muscles become weaker","Rib cage becomes more flexible","Alveoli become more elastic"],"answer":"Respiratory muscles become weaker"},
            {"question":"A decrease in gas exchange in older adults is related to:","options":["Thicker and more elastic alveoli","Thinner and less elastic alveoli","Increased respiratory muscle strength","Increased bronchiole elasticity"],"answer":"Thinner and less elastic alveoli"},
