            {"question":"Lack of economic security may cause older adults to:","options":["Lead full and active lives more easily","Avoid conserving their finances","Limit their use of health resources","Improve medication adherence automatically"],"answer":"Limit their use of health resources"},
            {"question":"Which of the following is listed as a common health problem among elderly people?","options":["Osteoarthritis","Fractures","Dental problems","All of the above"],"answer":"All of the above"},
            {"question":"Which combination contains only physical health problems listed in the lecture?","options":["Osteoarthritis, fractures, dental problems, impairment of special senses","Poverty, loneliness, isolation, generation gap","Depression, dementia, suicidal tendency, poverty","Diabetes, depression, isolation, cancer"],"answer":"Osteoarthritis, fractures, dental problems, impairment of special senses"},
            {"question":"Which cardiovascular problems are specifically listed among common health problems of elderly people?","options":["Cardiovascular disease and hypertension","Cardiovascular disease and hypotension only","Hypertension and anemia","Heart failure and arrhythmia only"],"answer":"Cardiovascular disease and hypertension"},
            {"question":"Which combination is listed among common health problems of elderly people?","options":["Hypothermia, cancer, and prostate enlargement","Asthma, migraine, and appendicitis","Pneumonia, gastritis, and hepatitis","Epilepsy, meningitis, and tuberculosis"],"answer":"Hypothermia, cancer, and prostate enlargement"},
            {"question":"Which of the following is listed as a common psychological problem among elderly people?","options":["Emotional problems and depression","Osteoarthritis","Hypertension","Dental problems"],"answer":"Emotional problems and depression"},
            {"question":"An elderly woman lives alone after the death of her spouse. She has become less interested in eating. Which factor BEST explains this change according to the lecture?","options":["Age-related decrease in metabolism","Psychological factors affecting the socialization of eating","Increased nutrient absorption","Increased appetite caused by medication"],"answer":"Psychological factors affecting the socialization of eating"},
            {"question":"An elderly patient has decreased taste and smell, poorly fitting dentures, and decreased nutrient absorption. Which interpretation is MOST appropriate?","options":["Several age-related factors are contributing to nutritional problems.","The problem is caused exclusively by low income.","The problem is caused exclusively by dementia.","These factors improve nutritional status."],"answer":"Several age-related factors are contributing to nutritional problems."},
