            {"question":"A nurse notices rubbish and objects scattered along the entrance walkway. Which intervention should be performed FIRST?","options":["Place a rug over the rubbish","Keep the walkway free of mess and rubbish","Reduce the lighting","Install a grab bar in the bathroom"],"answer":"Keep the walkway free of mess and rubbish"},
            {"question":"An elderly client's walking path contains an irregular surface. Which intervention is MOST appropriate?","options":["Ignore the area if the client has good vision","Fix the irregular area of the walking path","Cover it with loose rugs","Mark it only with furniture"],"answer":"Fix the irregular area of the walking path"},
            {"question":"An elderly client has impaired vision. Which combination is BEST for improving safety according to the lecture?","options":["Dim lighting and dark floor markings","Regular eye appointments, proper lighting, reduced glare, and bright-color markings","Avoiding all exercise and using loose rugs","Keeping the room cold and reducing lighting"],"answer":"Regular eye appointments, proper lighting, reduced glare, and bright-color markings"},
